<section class="hero">
  <h1>{{ club.tagline }}</h1>
  <p>{{ club.name }} has been helping people develop public speaking and
  leadership skills since {{ club.founded }}. Visit one of our meetings and
  see for yourself how Toastmasters helps people build confidence!</p>
  <a class="button" href="/membership/">Come along as a guest</a>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Visit</h2>
  <p>It is 100% free to visit as a guest and there is no pressure to speak
  at your first meeting. Simply come along and enjoy the speeches. If you'd
  rather join in, most guests are welcome to answer a Table Topics question
  or give a short introduction of themselves, but it's entirely up to you.
  We meet {{ club.meeting.frequency }}, {{ club.meeting.time }}, in the
  {{ club.meeting.venue }} ({{ club.meeting.address }}).</p>
  <p>Note: on the 4th Wednesday of the month we hold an online committee
  meeting ({{ club.committeeMeeting.time }}) rather than a regular guest
  meeting, see the schedule below.</p>
  <p>We're a welcoming bunch, and new members are paired with an experienced
  member as a mentor, so you'll always have someone to turn to with
  questions while you settle in.</p>

  <iframe
    class="map-embed"
    src="https://www.google.com/maps?q=Lincoln+Events+Centre,+15+Meijer+Drive,+Lincoln&output=embed"
    width="100%" height="300" style="border:0"
    loading="lazy"
    referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade"
    title="Map to {{ club.meeting.venue }}">
  </iframe>

  <h3>Meeting schedule</h3>
  <p>Scroll for the full published schedule, including meetings already
  held this year.</p>
  <ul id="upcoming-meetings"
      class="meeting-dates-list meeting-dates-scroll"
      data-meeting-time="{{ club.meeting.time }}"
      data-committee-time="{{ club.committeeMeeting.time }}">
    <li>Loading schedule&hellip;</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
  <div class="faq-list">
    <details>
      <summary>Do I have to speak at my first meeting?</summary>
      <p>No, speaking is entirely optional. Plenty of guests like to answer
      a Table Topics question or give a short introduction of themselves,
      but you're just as welcome to sit back and watch.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What should I wear?</summary>
      <p>Smart casual is fine, there's no dress code. Come as you are.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What actually happens at a meeting?</summary>
      <p>A mix of prepared speeches, impromptu "Table Topics" speaking, and
      constructive evaluations, run through a set of rotating member roles.
      See the <a href="/resources/">Resources page</a> for a full
      breakdown of each role.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Is it normal to be nervous about public speaking?</summary>
      <p>Completely. It's the single biggest reason people join Toastmasters
      in the first place, and everyone in the room has been exactly
      where you are.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can I bring a friend?</summary>
      <p>Of course, guests are always welcome, on your first visit or any time.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<script src="/js/meeting-dates.js" defer></script>
